// The Lantern Ward (M3 C1): a hub and three rooms of Jinzhou's kind, white plaster and charcoal tile, made of
// the town's builtins and materials and Kenney's hills. A first draft nobody has judged. Exit test 1 walks it from
// `player_start` to `boss`, through a fight in each room. No code names it: `--zone lantern_ward` finds it by its pack.
//
// A building or a length of wall that repeats is one mesh, placed in `instances`, so it costs the pack once. Small
// things are prefabs in `placements`, merged into their cells. `lantern_ward.colliders.ron` is what a body walks on and
// what the navmesh bakes from, and `lantern_ward.probes.ron` lists what the probe grid sees: moving something here moves
// it there too, which `tools/sapphire_pipeline/tests/zone_ward.rs` holds.
//
// Space: metres, +Y up. The hub is 40 m square about the origin, and a lane 9 m wide leaves it east, west and north.
// The Market Court lies east (x 44 to 84), the Blossom Garden west, the Temple Court north (z -60 to -116), its back
// 16 m a terrace 1.2 m up with the boss on it. Walls and rows close each place, so what's walkable is what's meant.
